0
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
If you give a mouse a cookie,

1
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:09,980
then it'll ask for a glass of milk.

2
00:00:09,983 --> 00:00:11,983
Then one thing will lead to another

3
00:00:11,983 --> 00:00:13,983
And you never know what's next

4
00:00:13,983 --> 00:00:15,983
Let's go to unexpected places

5
00:00:15,983 --> 00:00:17,983
They'll leave us smiling faces

6
00:00:17,983 --> 00:00:19,963
With Moose, Pig, Cat, and Dog

7
00:00:19,967 --> 00:00:21,507
So come on, come on.

8
00:00:22,007 --> 00:00:25,287
If you gave a mouse a cookie, you never know what you get.

9
00:00:25,747 --> 00:00:29,767
If you gave a mouse a cookie, what do you think will happen next?

10
00:00:29,951 --> 00:00:39,911
Thank you.

11
00:00:39,935 --> 00:00:42,275
I love laundry time.

12
00:00:42,395 --> 00:00:43,935
Can I help you put it away?

13
00:00:44,075 --> 00:00:45,275
Uh, sure.

14
00:00:48,575 --> 00:00:49,915
Mouse.

15
00:00:49,919 --> 00:00:52,459
That's not really helping.

16
00:00:52,459 --> 00:00:53,879
Can I have this sock?

17
00:00:53,879 --> 00:00:55,499
You don't wear socks.

18
00:00:55,499 --> 00:00:57,419
Just wait. Turn away.

19
00:00:57,419 --> 00:00:59,899
If you give a mess a sock,

20
00:00:59,903 --> 00:01:00,903
Then...

21
00:01:00,903 --> 00:01:01,903
OK, you can look.

22
00:01:03,903 --> 00:01:05,903
It's the perfect me-sized sleeping bag!

23
00:01:05,903 --> 00:01:06,903
It is!

24
00:01:06,903 --> 00:01:09,883
If a mouse uses a sock as a sleeping bag,

25
00:01:09,887 --> 00:01:11,547
Then he's going to say...

26
00:01:11,687 --> 00:01:13,587
Let's camp out in the backyard!

27
00:01:13,727 --> 00:01:14,567
Both of us!

28
00:01:14,687 --> 00:01:15,967
Great idea, Mouse.

29
00:01:16,087 --> 00:01:17,127
Only...

30
00:01:17,267 --> 00:01:17,967
What?

31
00:01:18,087 --> 00:01:19,867
You're going to need a really big sock.

32
00:01:19,871 --> 00:01:21,911
- I've got a better idea. - What?

33
00:01:22,011 --> 00:01:23,871
I'll show you. It's in the shed.

34
00:01:25,711 --> 00:01:27,871
If we're both camping out in the backyard,

35
00:01:27,971 --> 00:01:29,851
then I'm going to get out of here.

36
00:01:29,855 --> 00:01:32,195
a regular-sized sleeping bag for me.

37
00:01:33,695 --> 00:01:35,735
There's one in here somewhere.

38
00:01:35,835 --> 00:01:36,835
Wow!

39
00:01:38,535 --> 00:01:39,835
I love it in here.

40
00:01:39,839 --> 00:01:41,839
It's so full of stuff.

41
00:01:41,839 --> 00:01:43,839
I think there's a tent in here, too.

42
00:01:48,839 --> 00:01:49,819
Oh!

43
00:01:49,823 --> 00:01:51,323
What's this?

44
00:01:51,323 --> 00:01:52,323
Don't pull that!

45
00:01:52,323 --> 00:01:53,323
That's--

46
00:01:53,323 --> 00:01:54,323
Whoa!

47
00:01:54,323 --> 00:01:56,323
The self-inflating raft.

48
00:01:56,323 --> 00:01:59,803
Does self-inflating mean it blows itself out?

49
00:01:59,807 --> 00:02:01,307
Uh, yeah.

50
00:02:01,307 --> 00:02:04,807
Did I just hear a self-inflating raft?

51
00:02:04,807 --> 00:02:07,807
Oliver and I are going camping in the backyard.

52
00:02:07,807 --> 00:02:09,787
I inflated the raft.

53
00:02:09,791 --> 00:02:13,291
Wait, did you say camping in the backyard?

54
00:02:13,291 --> 00:02:14,291
That's right.

55
00:02:14,291 --> 00:02:16,291
If I hear someone's camping,

56
00:02:16,291 --> 00:02:19,791
then I just have to go camping too.

57
00:02:19,775 --> 00:02:20,975
Can I camp out with you guys?

58
00:02:21,115 --> 00:02:21,615
Sure.

59
00:02:21,735 --> 00:02:22,615
The more the merrier.

60
00:02:22,735 --> 00:02:25,155
Ooh, the more the merrier.

61
00:02:25,275 --> 00:02:26,655
That gives me an idea.

62
00:02:26,775 --> 00:02:27,655
See you later.

63
00:02:28,615 --> 00:02:29,755
Let's get this tense.

64
00:02:29,759 --> 00:02:31,759
- Put it over there.

65
00:02:33,759 --> 00:02:37,759
- Hmm, it looks like there are some poles that go up.

66
00:02:37,759 --> 00:02:39,739
Or maybe down?

67
00:02:39,743 --> 00:02:42,583
Have no fear, Oliver. I'll take care of it.

68
00:02:44,583 --> 00:02:46,083
Yep, and this goes...

69
00:02:46,083 --> 00:02:47,083
Whoops.

70
00:02:47,083 --> 00:02:48,043
Now we can...

71
00:02:48,043 --> 00:02:49,723
Uh-oh. Oh, there's the problem.

72
00:02:49,727 --> 00:02:50,227
And then--

73
00:02:50,227 --> 00:02:51,027
Ah!

74
00:02:51,027 --> 00:02:53,027
Tell me when it's safe to look.

75
00:02:53,027 --> 00:02:55,127
OK, you can look now.

76
00:02:55,127 --> 00:02:56,527
Oh, can I have that?

77
00:02:56,527 --> 00:02:57,527
Sure.

78
00:02:57,527 --> 00:02:59,707
Why?

79
00:02:59,711 --> 00:03:01,211
Wee!

80
00:03:01,211 --> 00:03:04,711
Ah, now we each have our own tent.

81
00:03:04,711 --> 00:03:05,711
Bah!

82
00:03:05,711 --> 00:03:07,691
Oops.

83
00:03:07,691 --> 00:03:09,691
Heh.

84
00:03:09,695 --> 00:03:12,695
Here you go.

85
00:03:12,695 --> 00:03:13,695
What's this?

86
00:03:13,695 --> 00:03:16,695
The invitation to your campout, of course.

87
00:03:16,695 --> 00:03:19,675
You did say, "The more the merrier."

88
00:03:19,679 --> 00:03:21,679
Oliver, we're invited!

89
00:03:21,679 --> 00:03:25,679
I have everything we need for a perfect campout.

90
00:03:25,679 --> 00:03:29,659
Tents, board games, guitar, pretend campfire, ice bar.

91
00:03:29,663 --> 00:03:31,823
Circle hammer, obviously.

92
00:03:31,823 --> 00:03:33,663
Cooler lanterns and trash bags

93
00:03:33,663 --> 00:03:37,123
so we can leave the campground as clean as we found it.

94
00:03:37,123 --> 00:03:39,643
Pig makes more lists than you do, Oliver.

95
00:03:39,647 --> 00:03:41,147
Cat!

96
00:03:41,247 --> 00:03:42,747
I'm here for the camp out.

97
00:03:42,847 --> 00:03:44,687
The invitation said three on the dot.

98
00:03:44,787 --> 00:03:45,647
Am I late?

99
00:03:45,747 --> 00:03:46,647
Nope.

100
00:03:46,747 --> 00:03:47,247
I'm here.

101
00:03:47,347 --> 00:03:48,647
I'm coming.

102
00:03:48,747 --> 00:03:49,627
Did I make a mistake?

103
00:03:49,631 --> 00:03:51,671
Is the camp out over? Is it the next day already?

104
00:03:51,671 --> 00:03:53,671
I did, I missed it, didn't I?

105
00:03:53,671 --> 00:03:55,671
We haven't even started.

106
00:03:55,671 --> 00:03:59,611
Yay! Oh, I'm so happy we're all camping!

107
00:03:59,615 --> 00:04:01,615
This is so exciting!

108
00:04:01,615 --> 00:04:03,615
But where's Moose?

109
00:04:03,615 --> 00:04:05,615
Oh, he says he might not come.

110
00:04:05,615 --> 00:04:07,615
I wonder why.

111
00:04:07,615 --> 00:04:09,615
Maybe we'd better ask him.

112
00:04:09,599 --> 00:04:12,099
- Moose! - Hi, Mouse.

113
00:04:12,099 --> 00:04:13,439
Hi, Oliver.

114
00:04:13,439 --> 00:04:15,559
We wanted to make sure you were coming to our camp out.

115
00:04:15,559 --> 00:04:17,559
- I'm sorry. - I'm sorry.

116
00:04:17,559 --> 00:04:19,559
- I'm sorry. - I'm sorry.

117
00:04:19,583 --> 00:04:29,563
Oh, camp away from home? In a dark tent? With all those scary noises? Why don't you go without me?

118
00:04:29,567 --> 00:04:31,607
Moose, we don't want to camp without you.

119
00:04:31,727 --> 00:04:33,607
Are you scared to go camping?

120
00:04:33,747 --> 00:04:36,647
Mmm, a little.

121
00:04:36,767 --> 00:04:37,647
Hey, Leo.

122
00:04:37,767 --> 00:04:39,547
Moose has a heart.

123
00:04:39,551 --> 00:04:43,551
staying in new places, don't you, Moose?

124
00:04:43,551 --> 00:04:45,551
Being away from home can be hard.

125
00:04:45,551 --> 00:04:46,551
I know.

126
00:04:46,551 --> 00:04:48,551
But we'll just be in our backyard.

127
00:04:48,551 --> 00:04:49,531
And if you need any help,

128
00:04:49,535 --> 00:04:51,535
Just call and I'll hop right over.

129
00:04:51,535 --> 00:04:53,535
Why are you hopping on one foot?

130
00:04:53,535 --> 00:04:55,535
I'm trying to break my record!

131
00:04:55,535 --> 00:04:58,535
So far, I'm up to 178 hops.

132
00:04:59,519 --> 00:05:01,019
- 179.

133
00:05:01,019 --> 00:05:04,319
- Well, I think I'll feel okay about camping out

134
00:05:04,319 --> 00:05:06,359
if I can bring along my lovey.

135
00:05:06,359 --> 00:05:09,499
- Great, let's go.

136
00:05:09,503 --> 00:05:16,503
Oh, you're just in time. Check out what I've done with the place.

137
00:05:16,503 --> 00:05:19,483
Ooh.

138
00:05:19,487 --> 00:05:23,627
If I'm camping out, then I like to do it in style.

139
00:05:24,167 --> 00:05:26,727
There's nothing like roughing it in the great outdoors.

140
00:05:29,471 --> 00:05:31,471
Cool.

141
00:05:31,471 --> 00:05:33,471
Look at me!

142
00:05:33,471 --> 00:05:34,471
I'm in! I'm out!

143
00:05:34,471 --> 00:05:35,471
I'm in! I'm out again!

144
00:05:35,471 --> 00:05:37,471
Oh, tents are the best thing ever!

145
00:05:37,471 --> 00:05:39,451
I can go in or out whenever I need them!

146
00:05:39,455 --> 00:05:41,115
I feel like it.

147
00:05:41,115 --> 00:05:43,455
And this one's for you, Moose.

148
00:05:43,455 --> 00:05:44,455
Really?

149
00:05:44,455 --> 00:05:45,755
For me?

150
00:05:45,755 --> 00:05:46,995
How nice.

151
00:05:46,995 --> 00:05:49,435
Let the camp out begin.

152
00:05:49,439 --> 00:05:50,279
- Yeah!

153
00:05:50,279 --> 00:05:51,099
- Woo-hoo!

154
00:05:51,099 --> 00:05:51,939
- Woo-hoo!

155
00:05:51,939 --> 00:05:52,779
- Woo-hoo!

156
00:05:52,779 --> 00:05:55,099
- Okay, if we're camping out,

157
00:05:55,099 --> 00:05:58,819
then we definitely need to play hide and seek.

158
00:05:58,819 --> 00:05:59,419
- 95.

159
00:05:59,423 --> 00:06:04,423
95, 96, 97, 98, 99, 100.

160
00:06:05,623 --> 00:06:09,403
Ready or not, here I come.

161
00:06:09,407 --> 00:06:19,387
- Aha! - Aha!

162
00:06:19,391 --> 00:06:21,391
Hmm.

163
00:06:21,391 --> 00:06:24,391
Now where could everyone be?

164
00:06:24,391 --> 00:06:27,391
That sounds like dog.

165
00:06:27,391 --> 00:06:29,371
Where is he?

166
00:06:29,375 --> 00:06:31,375
Whoa! Ooh, that tickles!

167
00:06:31,375 --> 00:06:32,875
- -Bah!

168
00:06:32,875 --> 00:06:34,455
-Dog! -You found me!

169
00:06:34,455 --> 00:06:36,755
That was a really good hiding place.

170
00:06:36,755 --> 00:06:39,355
Oh, thanks, Mouse.

171
00:06:39,359 --> 00:06:45,359
Hmm, where could the rest of them be?

172
00:06:46,359 --> 00:06:47,359
Not here.

173
00:06:47,359 --> 00:06:49,339
Not here. Thanks, log.

174
00:06:49,343 --> 00:06:51,343
Nothing here but a talking log.

175
00:06:53,343 --> 00:06:55,343
A talking log? Hang on.

176
00:06:56,343 --> 00:06:57,343
Gotcha!

177
00:06:57,343 --> 00:06:59,323
You found me.

178
00:06:59,327 --> 00:07:00,327
Hello, cat.

179
00:07:04,327 --> 00:07:06,327
Hmm, someone has to be here.

180
00:07:06,327 --> 00:07:07,327
Did I hear something?

181
00:07:07,327 --> 00:07:09,307
Nothing here.

182
00:07:09,311 --> 00:07:12,311
Wow, I never knew we had a tree that grew shoes.

183
00:07:12,311 --> 00:07:14,311
Or that giggles.

184
00:07:14,311 --> 00:07:17,311
Hey, you're no tree, you're Oliver.

185
00:07:17,311 --> 00:07:19,291
You guys are so cute.

186
00:07:19,295 --> 00:07:20,295
You got me.

187
00:07:24,295 --> 00:07:25,795
Hmm, wait a minute.

188
00:07:25,795 --> 00:07:27,675
Flowers don't have ears.

189
00:07:27,675 --> 00:07:29,275
I see you, pig.

190
00:07:29,279 --> 00:07:31,279
Yeah, that was amazing!

191
00:07:31,279 --> 00:07:32,619
Did you find everyone?

192
00:07:32,619 --> 00:07:34,959
Everybody, except Moose.

193
00:07:34,959 --> 00:07:37,579
I wonder where he went.

194
00:07:37,579 --> 00:07:39,259
I think I know.

195
00:07:39,263 --> 00:07:44,263
- Moose?

196
00:07:44,263 --> 00:07:46,263
- Um, I'm not here.

197
00:07:47,263 --> 00:07:49,243
- Yes, you are.

198
00:07:49,247 --> 00:07:51,247
That's a really good hiding place.

199
00:07:51,247 --> 00:07:54,047
Oh, oh, um, yeah, thanks.

200
00:07:54,047 --> 00:07:57,087
Maybe I'll just hide here a little longer if you don't mind.

201
00:07:57,087 --> 00:07:59,227
Like, 'til morning?

202
00:07:59,231 --> 00:08:03,031
But if you stay here, then you'll miss the camp out.

203
00:08:03,111 --> 00:08:05,231
Yeah, but it'll be less scary.

204
00:08:05,311 --> 00:08:07,771
Aw, you're still scared, huh?

205
00:08:07,851 --> 00:08:09,211
314?

206
00:08:09,215 --> 00:08:10,875
315.

207
00:08:10,875 --> 00:08:13,915
Moose, would bringing something else from your room

208
00:08:13,915 --> 00:08:16,715
make you feel safer at the camp out?

209
00:08:16,715 --> 00:08:18,015
Yeah.

210
00:08:18,015 --> 00:08:19,195
Well, what would you like?

211
00:08:19,199 --> 00:08:20,859
- What do you like?

212
00:08:20,859 --> 00:08:25,039
- Um, my stuffies, my vase of flowers,

213
00:08:25,039 --> 00:08:29,179
my chest, um, my gardening hat.

214
00:08:29,183 --> 00:08:32,183
Aw, you guys are the best.

215
00:08:32,183 --> 00:08:34,683
Here's my favorite campout song.

216
00:08:34,683 --> 00:08:37,183
The sun is setting low.

217
00:08:37,183 --> 00:08:39,163
It's really quite a sight.

218
00:08:39,167 --> 00:08:42,167
Enjoy the sunlight as it fades

219
00:08:42,167 --> 00:08:45,167
'Cause it's gonna be dark tonight

220
00:08:45,167 --> 00:08:48,167
Yes, it's getting dark tonight

221
00:08:48,167 --> 00:08:49,147
Oh, it's gonna be dark

222
00:08:49,151 --> 00:08:51,151
It's gonna be dark tonight

223
00:08:51,151 --> 00:08:53,151
Find a friend and snuggle up tight

224
00:08:53,151 --> 00:08:55,151
'Cause it's gonna be dark tonight

225
00:08:55,151 --> 00:08:57,151
Dark, dark, dark, dark

226
00:08:57,151 --> 00:08:59,131
Can't see a thing out of it

227
00:08:59,135 --> 00:09:04,135
'Cause it's really, really dark tonight.

228
00:09:07,135 --> 00:09:09,115
- Moose, are you ready?

229
00:09:09,119 --> 00:09:10,959
- Are you feeling okay? - Me?

230
00:09:10,959 --> 00:09:14,459
Oh, well, sometimes the dark makes me a little scared.

231
00:09:14,459 --> 00:09:16,959
Yeah, dark can be scary.

232
00:09:16,959 --> 00:09:19,099
I have just the thing.

233
00:09:19,103 --> 00:09:21,103
It'll make the dark go away.

234
00:09:21,103 --> 00:09:23,103
Four hundred and twelve, four hundred and thirteen,

235
00:09:23,103 --> 00:09:26,103
four hundred and fourteen, four hundred and fifteen.

236
00:09:26,103 --> 00:09:29,083
Lantern!

237
00:09:29,087 --> 00:09:29,927
- Ooh.

238
00:09:32,667 --> 00:09:34,887
- Much better, right Moose?

239
00:09:34,887 --> 00:09:39,067
- Oh yes, and you know, if I have a lantern then,

240
00:09:39,071 --> 00:09:39,911
- What?

241
00:09:39,911 --> 00:09:41,071
- You guys sit over there.

242
00:09:41,071 --> 00:09:42,071
I'll show you.

243
00:09:47,071 --> 00:09:49,051
I just didn't know.

244
00:09:49,055 --> 00:09:51,055
have to make shadow puppets.

245
00:09:53,055 --> 00:09:55,055
It's people climbing a mountain.

246
00:09:57,055 --> 00:09:59,035
And when they get to the gym,

247
00:09:59,039 --> 00:10:03,039
On top of the mountain, a carousel!

248
00:10:03,039 --> 00:10:05,039
Ooh!

249
00:10:05,039 --> 00:10:07,039
518, 519.

250
00:10:07,039 --> 00:10:09,019
Ooh, and after they ride,

251
00:10:09,023 --> 00:10:12,523
Inside the carousel, they go and visit a castle.

252
00:10:12,523 --> 00:10:16,023
Then they go inside and meet the king.

253
00:10:18,023 --> 00:10:19,003
The king says,

254
00:10:19,007 --> 00:10:21,967
Hi, did you like my carousel?

255
00:10:22,207 --> 00:10:23,967
Yes, oh yes we did.

256
00:10:24,307 --> 00:10:27,007
Then they go down the mountain, the end.

257
00:10:27,007 --> 00:10:28,007
Yeah!

258
00:10:28,991 --> 00:10:32,491
Thank you! Thank you! You're too kind!

259
00:10:32,491 --> 00:10:34,991
That was incredible, Moose!

260
00:10:34,991 --> 00:10:38,971
Doing a puppet show makes me feel much better about camping out.

261
00:10:38,975 --> 00:10:42,475
At least your tent should feel like home now.

262
00:10:42,475 --> 00:10:45,055
Wow, it does!

263
00:10:45,055 --> 00:10:46,715
698?

264
00:10:46,715 --> 00:10:48,955
699?

265
00:10:48,959 --> 00:10:53,959
700! Yes! 700 hops on one foot!

266
00:10:54,039 --> 00:10:55,259
A new record!

267
00:10:55,339 --> 00:10:56,799
Congratulations, Leo!

268
00:10:56,879 --> 00:10:58,939
It's about time for bed.

269
00:10:58,943 --> 00:11:00,443
Ready for lights out?

270
00:11:00,443 --> 00:11:02,143
I am now.

271
00:11:02,143 --> 00:11:03,643
Thanks, everyone.

272
00:11:05,783 --> 00:11:07,323
- Good night, everybody.

273
00:11:07,323 --> 00:11:08,923
- Good night.

274
00:11:08,927 --> 00:11:10,927
I'm glad we had a campout, Oliver.

275
00:11:10,927 --> 00:11:13,427
Me too. Let's get in our sleeping bags.

276
00:11:13,427 --> 00:11:15,267
I only need one thing.

277
00:11:15,267 --> 00:11:16,427
Gotcha covered.

278
00:11:16,427 --> 00:11:18,907
The sock! Thank you.

279
00:11:18,911 --> 00:11:22,911
- Um, I think I'll sleep in your tent.

280
00:11:22,911 --> 00:11:23,911
- Great.

281
00:11:24,911 --> 00:11:28,891
If you give a mouse a sock, what do you think will happen

282
00:11:28,895 --> 00:11:29,395
Next.

283
00:11:38,879 --> 00:11:43,879
And Mouse is up at bat.

284
00:11:43,879 --> 00:11:48,879
He's going to knock this one out of the...

285
00:11:48,863 --> 00:11:49,703
-Bed.

286
00:11:49,703 --> 00:11:53,863
-Softball jersey, cap, pants, mitt.

287
00:11:53,863 --> 00:11:56,863
I think that's everything I need for the softball game.

288
00:11:56,863 --> 00:11:58,843
Why do I feel like I'm forgetting that?

289
00:11:58,847 --> 00:12:00,847
- Mouse swings.

290
00:12:00,847 --> 00:12:02,847
He's gonna catch the ball.

291
00:12:02,847 --> 00:12:04,847
He's got it, he's got it, he's--

292
00:12:04,847 --> 00:12:05,847
Oliver!

293
00:12:05,847 --> 00:12:07,847
- Yes, Mouse? - I need a sock.

294
00:12:07,847 --> 00:12:08,827
I need a sock.

295
00:12:08,831 --> 00:12:09,671
Quick!

296
00:12:10,291 --> 00:12:11,171
Here you go.

297
00:12:13,211 --> 00:12:16,331
If you give him us a sock, then...

298
00:12:16,331 --> 00:12:18,811
he's gonna want to use it as a softball mitt.

299
00:12:18,815 --> 00:12:20,655
- Caught it!

300
00:12:20,655 --> 00:12:23,115
And the crowd goes wild!

301
00:12:23,115 --> 00:12:25,115
- Wait, that's what I forgot.

302
00:12:25,115 --> 00:12:26,575
I team socks.

303
00:12:26,575 --> 00:12:28,795
I think they're still in the dryer.

304
00:12:28,799 --> 00:12:30,799
Oh, where is it?

305
00:12:30,799 --> 00:12:32,799
I can't find it.

306
00:12:32,799 --> 00:12:34,799
I can only find one.

307
00:12:34,799 --> 00:12:36,799
That's my ride to the beach.

308
00:12:36,799 --> 00:12:38,799
Oh, my gosh.

309
00:12:38,783 --> 00:12:40,083
I've got to go!

310
00:12:40,183 --> 00:12:43,323
But Oliver, you can't play wearing just one of your team's socks.

311
00:12:43,423 --> 00:12:45,083
I'll find your missing sock and bring it to you

312
00:12:45,183 --> 00:12:46,523
before the game starts.

313
00:12:46,623 --> 00:12:47,623
Thanks, Mouse.

314
00:12:47,723 --> 00:12:48,763
You're the best.

315
00:12:48,767 --> 00:12:50,107
See you later.

316
00:12:50,107 --> 00:12:54,727
Now, if I were a sock, where would I hide?

317
00:12:54,727 --> 00:12:58,747
Ha ha ha ha ha!

318
00:12:58,751 --> 00:13:00,751
Nope, sock's not here.

319
00:13:07,451 --> 00:13:08,731
Nope!

320
00:13:08,735 --> 00:13:10,075
It's dusty back here.

321
00:13:16,915 --> 00:13:17,735
Aha!

322
00:13:17,735 --> 00:13:18,715
The sock!

323
00:13:18,719 --> 00:13:21,759
Now I wonder how I got between the couch cushion.

324
00:13:21,759 --> 00:13:22,759
Oh yeah!

325
00:13:22,759 --> 00:13:25,759
I used it as a pillow when I took a nap here yesterday.

326
00:13:25,759 --> 00:13:26,659
Oops.

327
00:13:26,659 --> 00:13:28,699
But the important thing is to get it to Oliver in time for the

328
00:13:28,703 --> 00:13:31,743
It's a big game, but how?

329
00:13:31,743 --> 00:13:33,783
I know who I can ask.

330
00:13:38,687 --> 00:13:40,687
Hi, Mouse.

331
00:13:40,687 --> 00:13:41,687
Hi, Pig.

332
00:13:41,687 --> 00:13:43,687
I've got to get this very important special team sock

333
00:13:43,687 --> 00:13:45,687
to Oliver for his big game.

334
00:13:45,687 --> 00:13:47,687
Will you drive me there on your scooter?

335
00:13:47,687 --> 00:13:48,667
Aye.

336
00:13:48,671 --> 00:13:51,711
I'm always looking for a chance to ride my scooter.

337
00:13:51,711 --> 00:13:52,711
Come on.

338
00:13:54,471 --> 00:13:55,471
Let's go, Pig.

339
00:13:55,471 --> 00:13:58,651
We've got a very important sock to deliver in time and time.

340
00:13:58,655 --> 00:14:00,655
Let me just straighten out the mirror.

341
00:14:00,655 --> 00:14:02,655
Definitely straight.

342
00:14:02,655 --> 00:14:06,655
Okay, now just gotta make sure the tires are full of air.

343
00:14:08,639 --> 00:14:10,719
Uh-huh. Tires are good.

344
00:14:10,899 --> 00:14:11,379
All right!

345
00:14:11,579 --> 00:14:11,919
Wait!

346
00:14:12,079 --> 00:14:12,479
What?

347
00:14:13,039 --> 00:14:15,079
I've just got to clean off this bit of dirt.

348
00:14:15,299 --> 00:14:18,059
But it's tiny. I can hardly see it. Can't it wait?

349
00:14:18,219 --> 00:14:18,539
Mouse.

350
00:14:18,623 --> 00:14:21,623
We can't be riding around town with a dirty scooter.

351
00:14:21,703 --> 00:14:23,923
I just need something to clean it with.

352
00:14:24,003 --> 00:14:25,003
Use this!

353
00:14:25,083 --> 00:14:26,423
Just use the toe, though.

354
00:14:26,503 --> 00:14:28,603
We don't want to get Oliver's special team socked.

355
00:14:28,607 --> 00:14:30,607
- Perfect. Ready to go.

356
00:14:36,607 --> 00:14:38,587
- Ah, nice.

357
00:14:38,591 --> 00:14:42,591
Something like a scooter mission on a brisk day.

358
00:14:42,591 --> 00:14:44,591
Uh, too brisk.

359
00:14:44,591 --> 00:14:46,591
Huh, a scarf.

360
00:14:46,591 --> 00:14:48,571
Nice and toasty.

361
00:14:48,575 --> 00:14:49,735
really comes in handy.

362
00:14:49,835 --> 00:14:54,115
And my trusty scooter will get us to Oliver's game in no time.

363
00:14:55,375 --> 00:14:56,815
- Pig? - Yes, Mouse?

364
00:14:57,755 --> 00:14:58,555
What's that sound?

365
00:14:58,559 --> 00:15:00,559
And why are we slowing down?

366
00:15:00,559 --> 00:15:03,559
Uh, nothing to worry about.

367
00:15:03,559 --> 00:15:07,559
It's just, well, we seem to be running out of gas.

368
00:15:07,559 --> 00:15:08,539
What does that mean?

369
00:15:08,543 --> 00:15:12,043
Um, if the scooter runs out of gas, then...

370
00:15:14,463 --> 00:15:16,423
It doesn't go.

371
00:15:16,503 --> 00:15:18,523
But what do we do?

372
00:15:18,527 --> 00:15:21,107
We've got to get this sock to Oliver at the game!

373
00:15:21,147 --> 00:15:24,067
Well, you said the sock comes in handy.

374
00:15:24,107 --> 00:15:26,147
Maybe it'll come in handy now.

375
00:15:26,187 --> 00:15:26,867
How?

376
00:15:26,907 --> 00:15:28,507
Oh, may I?

377
00:15:28,511 --> 00:15:32,511
To flag down, help.

378
00:15:32,511 --> 00:15:33,511
This is terrible.

379
00:15:33,511 --> 00:15:35,511
If we don't reach Oliver with the sock,

380
00:15:35,511 --> 00:15:36,511
then he'll have to play...

381
00:15:36,511 --> 00:15:38,491
Without it!

382
00:15:38,495 --> 00:15:40,495
Dog! Oh, thank goodness.

383
00:15:40,495 --> 00:15:42,495
I came as soon as I saw your flag.

384
00:15:42,495 --> 00:15:44,495
Uh, sock?

385
00:15:44,495 --> 00:15:46,495
What's going on?

386
00:15:46,495 --> 00:15:48,475
We need to get to the school first.

387
00:15:48,479 --> 00:15:50,399
for Oliver's big softball game.

388
00:15:50,399 --> 00:15:52,179
And Pig's scooter broke down.

389
00:15:52,179 --> 00:15:54,479
- Well, I just saw Moose.

390
00:15:54,479 --> 00:15:55,999
I bet he could give you a ride.

391
00:15:55,999 --> 00:15:56,919
- Great idea.

392
00:15:56,919 --> 00:15:58,459
We can ask Moose for a ride on his back.

393
00:15:58,463 --> 00:15:59,803
Where did you see him?

394
00:15:59,803 --> 00:16:01,803
It was this way.

395
00:16:01,803 --> 00:16:06,303
No, it was this way.

396
00:16:06,303 --> 00:16:08,443
Hang on.

397
00:16:08,447 --> 00:16:09,487
I smell muffins.

398
00:16:09,847 --> 00:16:12,227
And where there's muffins, there's usually a moose.

399
00:16:12,627 --> 00:16:13,387
Follow me.

400
00:16:14,387 --> 00:16:14,927
Oh, yeah.

401
00:16:18,431 --> 00:16:20,431
There he is!

402
00:16:22,431 --> 00:16:24,431
Oh, hi, Mouse. Hi, Pig. Hi, Dog.

403
00:16:24,431 --> 00:16:26,431
-Hi, Moose. -Moose, we've got a problem.

404
00:16:26,431 --> 00:16:28,411
What is it?

405
00:16:28,415 --> 00:16:32,415
Oliver's only wearing one special team sock for his big game.

406
00:16:32,415 --> 00:16:33,415
Oh, dear.

407
00:16:33,415 --> 00:16:35,415
So do you think you could give us a ride to the school

408
00:16:35,415 --> 00:16:37,415
so I can give him the other one?

409
00:16:37,415 --> 00:16:38,395
Of course.

410
00:16:38,399 --> 00:16:40,699
Of course, I'd be happy to take you to the game.

411
00:16:40,699 --> 00:16:43,899
But first, I promise to do a puppet show for the kids.

412
00:16:43,899 --> 00:16:46,319
The story of Little Red Riding Hood.

413
00:16:46,319 --> 00:16:48,379
Little Red Riding Hood?

414
00:16:48,383 --> 00:16:49,883
Oh, I love that story.

415
00:16:49,883 --> 00:16:52,143
She takes a basket of goodies to her grandma,

416
00:16:52,143 --> 00:16:55,023
and the big bad wolf tries to get them from her.

417
00:16:55,023 --> 00:16:57,103
It's very dramatic.

418
00:16:57,103 --> 00:16:58,363
Ooh, sounds exciting.

419
00:16:58,367 --> 00:17:02,367
It would be, except I have a problem.

420
00:17:02,367 --> 00:17:03,367
What?

421
00:17:03,367 --> 00:17:06,367
I forgot the big bad wolf puppet.

422
00:17:06,367 --> 00:17:07,367
Oh, no.

423
00:17:07,367 --> 00:17:08,347
That won't do.

424
00:17:08,351 --> 00:17:10,011
Oh, not good. Not good at all.

425
00:17:10,111 --> 00:17:13,431
I know! I can't tell the Little Red Riding Hood story

426
00:17:13,531 --> 00:17:15,351
without the Big Bad Wolf.

427
00:17:15,451 --> 00:17:17,351
When's a puppet show gonna start?

428
00:17:17,451 --> 00:17:18,331
I hope so.

429
00:17:18,335 --> 00:17:23,335
- Folks, there's just a slight technical problem,

430
00:17:25,375 --> 00:17:28,315
but the show will start very soon, I promise.

431
00:17:28,319 --> 00:17:31,819
I need a Big Bad Wolf puppet and I need it fast.

432
00:17:31,819 --> 00:17:34,119
- Oh, I have an idea for who can play Big Bad Wolf.

433
00:17:34,119 --> 00:17:35,119
- Who?

434
00:17:35,119 --> 00:17:36,619
- I'll give you a hint.

435
00:17:36,619 --> 00:17:38,299
He's small, just small.

436
00:17:38,303 --> 00:17:40,643
- Just about puppet-sized.

437
00:17:40,643 --> 00:17:44,303
- If you leave your big bad wolf puppet at home then,

438
00:17:44,303 --> 00:17:47,143
it's good to have a puppet-sized mouse

439
00:17:47,143 --> 00:17:48,283
who can play the part for you.

440
00:17:48,287 --> 00:17:50,287
Sorry about the delay.

441
00:17:50,287 --> 00:17:52,287
The show's about to start now.

442
00:17:55,287 --> 00:17:56,287
La la la!

443
00:17:56,287 --> 00:17:58,287
I'm little.

444
00:17:58,271 --> 00:18:01,271
And I'm on my way to my grandma's house.

445
00:18:01,271 --> 00:18:03,271
Oh, who are you?

446
00:18:03,271 --> 00:18:06,271
I'm the big bad wolf.

447
00:18:06,271 --> 00:18:08,251
And what do you have for me?

448
00:18:08,255 --> 00:18:10,595
in that basket. It looks yummy.

449
00:18:10,595 --> 00:18:14,595
It's goodies for my grandma. Gotta go now.

450
00:18:14,595 --> 00:18:18,235
Hmm. I'm going to follow her to grandma's and get her basket

451
00:18:18,239 --> 00:18:19,739
of goodies for myself.

452
00:18:19,739 --> 00:18:21,239
Bwahahahaha!

453
00:18:21,239 --> 00:18:22,239
Awww!

454
00:18:26,239 --> 00:18:28,219
Hello, I'm a little inchworm.

455
00:18:28,223 --> 00:18:30,723
And I'm going to save Little Red Riding Hood

456
00:18:30,723 --> 00:18:32,563
from the big bad wolf.

457
00:18:32,563 --> 00:18:33,563
Inchworm?

458
00:18:33,563 --> 00:18:38,203
But-- but there's no inchworm in Little Red Riding Hood?

459
00:18:38,207 --> 00:18:41,207
If you put a mouse in your puppet show,

460
00:18:41,207 --> 00:18:45,207
then he's going to want to change the story.

461
00:18:45,207 --> 00:18:48,187
Only I'm so sweet.

462
00:18:48,191 --> 00:18:52,271
Whoa, I'll never get there in time to save Little Red.

463
00:18:52,271 --> 00:18:54,331
But I know someone who can.

464
00:18:54,331 --> 00:18:58,171
I'll go get him.

465
00:18:58,175 --> 00:19:02,175
-

466
00:19:02,175 --> 00:19:04,175
- It's me, Mouse!

467
00:19:04,175 --> 00:19:07,175
I'm here to save Little Red from the big bad wolf.

468
00:19:07,175 --> 00:19:08,155
Here he comes.

469
00:19:08,159 --> 00:19:11,499
Shh, I'll hide and take him by surprise.

470
00:19:13,499 --> 00:19:15,659
I'm the big bad wolf.

471
00:19:15,759 --> 00:19:18,139
Look, here comes Little Red Riding Hood.

472
00:19:18,143 --> 00:19:25,143
I said, here comes Little Red Riding Hood.

473
00:19:25,143 --> 00:19:26,143
Oh, that's me.

474
00:19:26,143 --> 00:19:28,123
Sorry.

475
00:19:28,127 --> 00:19:32,127
Grandma, look! It's the big bad wolf!

476
00:19:32,127 --> 00:19:34,127
Oh, yeah!

477
00:19:34,127 --> 00:19:38,107
Grr! I'm going to take your basket of goods.

478
00:19:38,111 --> 00:19:40,111
Oh, no, you aren't.

479
00:19:40,111 --> 00:19:42,111
You're a little bitty mouse.

480
00:19:42,111 --> 00:19:44,111
How are you going to stop me?

481
00:19:44,111 --> 00:19:46,111
I'm gonna get you out of the way.

482
00:19:46,111 --> 00:19:48,091
You just tried.

483
00:19:48,095 --> 00:19:51,095
I might be little, but I'm strong.

484
00:19:51,095 --> 00:19:54,095
Grr to you!

485
00:19:54,095 --> 00:19:58,075
Get out of here and don't come back, big bad wolf!

486
00:19:58,079 --> 00:19:58,919
- Hey, Wolf.

487
00:20:02,519 --> 00:20:04,959
That Wolf won't bother you anymore.

488
00:20:04,959 --> 00:20:08,059
- Oh, thank you, Mouse.

489
00:20:08,063 --> 00:20:10,063
You're our hero!

490
00:20:11,063 --> 00:20:13,063
- Yeah! - Bravo!

491
00:20:13,063 --> 00:20:16,063
- Woo! - That mouse is so awesome!

492
00:20:16,063 --> 00:20:18,043
- Yeah, that was the best little reference

493
00:20:18,047 --> 00:20:21,507
- That writing good story I ever saw.

494
00:20:21,507 --> 00:20:23,007
- Oh, thank you, Mouse.

495
00:20:23,007 --> 00:20:24,927
You really saved the day.

496
00:20:24,927 --> 00:20:26,087
- You are amazing.

497
00:20:26,087 --> 00:20:28,027
So mouse-wolf-inchworm-like!

498
00:20:28,031 --> 00:20:30,071
How did you memorize all those lines?

499
00:20:30,071 --> 00:20:31,871
You were perfection.

500
00:20:31,871 --> 00:20:33,371
Oh, thanks.

501
00:20:33,371 --> 00:20:34,831
That's so nice.

502
00:20:34,831 --> 00:20:37,031
That sock really does come in so handy.

503
00:20:37,031 --> 00:20:38,011
Wait! The sock!

504
00:20:38,015 --> 00:20:40,855
We've got to go and get this to Oliver at the softball game.

505
00:20:40,855 --> 00:20:42,355
Hop on, everyone!

506
00:20:46,355 --> 00:20:47,995
Hey, that mouse just came out!

507
00:20:47,999 --> 00:20:49,999
They said they were going to a softball game.

508
00:20:49,999 --> 00:20:50,999
Let's go watch!

509
00:20:50,999 --> 00:20:51,999
Yeah!

510
00:20:51,999 --> 00:20:52,999
I want to go, too!

511
00:20:52,999 --> 00:20:53,999
I want to go, too!

512
00:20:55,999 --> 00:20:57,999
Guess no one's coming up.

513
00:20:57,983 --> 00:20:59,183
- I'm gonna watch the game.

514
00:20:59,183 --> 00:21:00,323
- It's too bad.

515
00:21:00,323 --> 00:21:01,323
- I know.

516
00:21:05,023 --> 00:21:06,323
- Hey guys, look.

517
00:21:06,323 --> 00:21:07,963
- Yeah!

518
00:21:07,967 --> 00:21:12,267
Mouse! You're here!

519
00:21:12,347 --> 00:21:14,767
I couldn't let you play the big game without this!

520
00:21:15,967 --> 00:21:17,947
Aw, thanks, Mouse.

521
00:21:17,951 --> 00:21:20,951
I'll put it on right now.

522
00:21:22,491 --> 00:21:24,491
Play ball!

523
00:21:24,491 --> 00:21:27,931
Gotta go play.

524
00:21:27,935 --> 00:21:35,235
That's Oliver.

525
00:21:35,735 --> 00:21:37,615
Yep, I brought him that left sock.

526
00:21:37,919 --> 00:21:47,899
- Yeah! Wow! - Yeah!

527
00:21:47,903 --> 00:21:48,743
- Yeah!

528
00:21:53,363 --> 00:21:54,783
- Go, Oliver!

529
00:21:54,783 --> 00:21:55,623
- Yeah!

530
00:21:56,823 --> 00:21:57,883
- Thanks, Mouse.

531
00:21:57,887 --> 00:22:00,387
You saved my left foot from being sockless

532
00:22:00,387 --> 00:22:02,487
and probably helped us win the game.

533
00:22:02,487 --> 00:22:04,187
- Aw, it was nothing.

534
00:22:04,187 --> 00:22:06,387
Ooh, it's a little chilly tonight.

535
00:22:06,387 --> 00:22:07,867
If I get chilly, then?

536
00:22:07,871 --> 00:22:11,171
It might be nice to have a hat to keep my ears warm.

537
00:22:11,211 --> 00:22:14,911
Hmm. I think I know what would work perfectly.

538
00:22:16,071 --> 00:22:17,851
How about a sock?

539
00:22:17,855 --> 00:22:19,855
Yes! A sock!

540
00:22:19,855 --> 00:22:24,855
There's nothing like a sock-stocking cap on a chilly night.

541
00:22:24,855 --> 00:22:27,835
Good night, Oliver.

542
00:22:27,839 --> 00:22:29,639
Good night, Mouse.

543
00:22:29,639 --> 00:22:32,719
If I give you a sock, what do you think will happen next?

544
00:22:36,479 --> 00:22:37,819
If you give a mouse a cookie,

545
00:22:37,823 --> 00:22:41,823
Then I'll ask for a glass of milk and then one thing will lead to another

546
00:22:41,823 --> 00:22:43,823
And you never know what's next

547
00:22:43,823 --> 00:22:45,823
Let's go to unexpected places

548
00:22:45,823 --> 00:22:47,803
They'll leave us smile every face

549
00:22:47,807 --> 00:22:57,787
We'll be right back.

